// Package jsonhandler serves an HTML form for editing a JSON value that a
// JSON Schema 2020-12 document describes, and turns the submitted form back
// into JSON that it validates against the schema.
//
// The form is server-rendered hypermedia. Edits such as adding an array
// item or choosing a oneOf variant are form submissions handled by
// [Handler.SubmitForm], so the form works without JavaScript; htmx
// attributes in the markup let it swap in place and validate as the user
// types when htmx is on the page. [TemplateRoutes], generated by muxt from
// routes.gohtml, registers the endpoints on an [net/http.ServeMux], and
// every endpoint responds with an HTML partial for another page to load or
// include.
//
// README.md documents the endpoints, how to put the form in an
// application, how schema keywords map to controls, the markup and its
// classes and data attributes (so a stylesheet can be written from scratch),
// the x-form annotations, and the starter stylesheet returned by
// [Stylesheet].
package jsonhandler
